Root cause:
The bug was caused by the `keyctl_restrict_keyring()` function allowing a NULL restriction string when a non-NULL type was specified. This led to a NULL pointer dereference in the `asymmetric_lookup_restriction()` function when it attempted to call `strcmp()` on the NULL restriction string. Since no key types utilize a NULL restriction meaningfully, the function was updated to reject a NULL restriction when a type is provided, preventing the dereference and potential crashes.
